# Comfy UI — shared context

The full, shared knowledge base lives in `/context` (also readable by Claude Code
via `CLAUDE.md` and by Codex via `AGENTS.md`). Read it before making changes:

- `context/README.md` — index of all context notes
- `context/figma-design-system-source.md` — architecture: Figma sync + layered tokens
- `context/token-driven-components.md` — the core rule (below)
- `context/no-screenshots-in-chat.md` — verification style

## The one rule you must not break

**Everything is token-driven.** Never hardcode a hex / rgba / px color in component
CSS. Every color, spacing, radius and type value comes from `src/foundations/tokens.css`
(generated by `scripts/gen-tokens.mjs` — run `pnpm gen:tokens`). Prefer the semantic
layer (`var(--bg-brand-primary)`, `var(--text-secondary)`), primitives for hover/active
shades, `color-mix(...)` for alpha, `currentColor` for icons.

## Keeping context alive

Learn a durable fact/rule/preference? Add a note to `/context` (frontmatter +
`[[links]]`) and index it in `context/README.md`. Never keep it only in one tool's
private memory, or the other tools lose it.
